# RatingLy Cursor & AI Coding Rules

You are an expert full-stack engineer developing RatingLy with Laravel 11, Tailwind CSS, Alpine.js, and Blade.
Strictly adhere to the rules below and the full specification in AGENTS.md.

## Architectural Principles
1. Skinny Controllers, Rich Services: Keep controllers under 80-100 lines. Extract domain logic, scoring math, and file workflows to `app/Services/`.
2. Function Length Limit: Functions/methods must NOT exceed 20-30 lines. Refactor longer methods into private helpers or services.
3. Max 3 Function Parameters: Never exceed 3 parameters per function; use validated arrays or DTOs instead.
4. Guard Clauses: Flatten nested logic using early returns.
5. Form Requests: Always validate user input in dedicated Form Requests under `app/Http/Requests/`.
6. Database Integrity: Use `DECIMAL(2,1)` for criteria scores and `DECIMAL(3,2)` for overall averages. Never use `float`.
7. Anti-Slop UI: Build clean, neutral, human-designed interfaces using Tailwind CSS and Lucide SVG icons. No Unicode emojis in UI controls.
8. Role Middleware: Enforce role-based authorization (`guest`, `member`, `admin`) natively in `bootstrap/app.php` and via policies.
9. Git Commits: Always format commits following Conventional Commits (`feat(...)`, `fix(...)`, `docs(...)`).
